course: dictionary
lesson: 8142
title: One person speaking for many
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A representative is a person who speaks or acts for other people. Your class might choose a representative to speak at the school council for everyone in the class. «A representative speaks for a group and also brings back what happened, including the other side's reasons.» So a representative speaks for the group and then reports back to it.
explain: The word has other meanings too. A sales representative works for a company and explains its products to people who might buy them. The meaning changes with the sentence, so check the clues around the word, just as you do with any new word.
explain: As an adjective, representative means typical: it shows what a whole group is like. «A representative sample» is a small group chosen so that it fairly shows the whole group. When you see "representative of" in a sentence, it is probably the adjective.
fact: A representative is a person who speaks or acts for others.
fact: «Representative» can also mean typical, as in «a representative sample».
fact: A representative sample is a small group that fairly shows the whole group.
fact: In the UK, elected representatives are called MPs, and they debate and vote on new laws in Parliament.
fact: In the United States, the lawmaking group is called Congress, and it has the House of Representatives and the Senate.
exercise: «A representative speaks for a group and also brings back what happened.» What is a representative? | A person who sells things in a shop | A group of children who all talk at once | A very old school building | *A person who speaks or acts for others
exercise: What does representative mean in «a representative sample»? | Very old and rare | Chosen by the teacher to be the best | *Typical, fairly showing what the whole group is like | The biggest group possible
exercise: «A sales representative explains a company's things to customers.» What job does this representative do? | Sits in Parliament and makes laws | Speaks for the class at the school council | Cleans the classroom windows | *Works for a company and explains its products
test: «Parliament is where elected representatives debate and vote on new laws.» In this sentence, what are representatives? | Books about laws | Rooms with green benches | Old castles on a hill | *People elected to debate and make laws
test: Which phrase uses representative as an adjective? | "our class representative" | *"a representative sample" | "a member of the House of Representatives" | "a sales representative"
exam: «Jada is our class representative.» What does Jada do? | Counts the sample | Sells the class's books | *Speaks for the whole class | Makes the class lunch
